{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NHhDFGyWvTTqMeqC7mhef1","type":"tool_result","content":"198:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dit\n199:- `px.col(g, c)`: set the fill color (px.* do it themselves)\n200:- `px.ddisc(g, cx, cy, r, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: soft disc that fades toward its edge (glows, smoke, dust): stepped alpha rings, or dithering in 'dither' style\n201:- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n202:- `px.dot(g, x, y, c)`: one pixel\n203:- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n204:- `px.glow(g, e = 1)`: GPU lighting: what follows glows (0..1). No effect in Canvas mode, so call it freely.\n205:- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n206:- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n207:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel off\n208:- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n209:- `px.reset(g)`: forget the color cache (after drawing on g with the canvas API directly)\n210:- `px.sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip = false)`: draw a sprite with its top-left corner at buffer pixel (x, y). flip mirrors it left-right; or o: { flip, rot (radians, turn\n360:- `E.font.default` †: the font used when none is named: 'normal' (5 x 7) or 'tiny' (3 x 5)\n361:- `E.font.height(lines = 1, o, lineGap)`: the height in pixels of that many lines (with o's scale and font, and lineGap between them)\n362:- `E.font.lineHeight(o)`: pixels from one line to the next\n363:- `E.font.text(g, s, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o = '#0b0814')`: draw text at (x, y) (its top-left; align: 'center' or 'right' moves it) in color. o\n364:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D\n365:- `E.font.width(s, o)`: width in pixels of the widest line. opts: a scale number or { font, scale }\n366:- `E.font.wrap(s, maxW, o)`: split text into lines no wider than maxW pixels\n1179:- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0\n1180:- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-\n1181:- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n1182:- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)\n170:- `E.mkCanvas(w, h)`: a new canvas of w x h pixels (scratch images and sprite sheets). With no document (Node: a headless game) a stand-in whose drawing does nothing,\n191:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward wa\n283:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that d\n300:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n309:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns tr\n345:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n486:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Sh\n489:- `game.freeze(s)`: hit-stop: the game stands still for s seconds (.04-.08 for a hit); input still ticks\nclass Menu {\n  constructor(game, items, o = {}) {\n    /** game: its game; items: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled }); i: the one under the cursor; active:\n     *  false stops it reading input */\n    this.game = game; this.items = items || []; this.i = 0; this.active = true;\n    /** x, y: where it sits, 'center' or pixels; title: a heading, or null; box: draw a window round it; color: the\n     *  entries' color; pick: the color of the one under the cursor; dim: disabled entries' color; bg, border: the\n     *  window's colors; onPick: called (i, item) on confirm; onCancel: called on cancel; onMove: called (i, item)\n     *  when the cursor moves; sound: false silences it; input: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so\n     *  any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's); scale: its text and rows that many times (2, 3:\n     *  across a room on a TV); rows: at most that many entries shown, the list scrolling under its cursor (0: all) */\n    Object.assign(this, { x: 'center', y: 'center', title: null, box: true, color: '#ffffff', pick: '#ffd36a', dim: '#6a6488', bg: '#141a3a', border: '#e8e4ff', onPick: null, onCancel: null, onMove: null, sound: true, input: null, scale: 1,\n    this._skip(1);\n  }\n  _label(it) { return typeof it === 'string' ? it : it.label; }\n  _off(it) { return typeof it === 'object' && it.disabled; }\n  _skip(dir) { for (let k = 0; k < this.items.length && this._off(this.items[this.i]); k++) this.i = (this.i + dir + this.items.length) % this.items.length; }\n  /** the entry under the cursor */\n  get selected() { return this.items[this.i]; }\n  // where it sits, from its items and the screen's size (update and draw both: a click picks an entry with no draw yet)\n  _layout() {\n    const S = this.game.screen, k = Math.max(1, Math.round(this.scale || 1)), fo = { scale: k }, labels = this.items.map(it => this._label(it)), n = labels.length;\n    const w = Math.max(E.font.width(this.title || '', fo), ...labels.map(l => E.font.width(l, fo))) + 22 * k, rowH = E.font.lineHeight(fo) + 2 * k, vis = this.rows > 0 ? Math.min(n, this.rows) : n;\n    let first = clamp(this._first || 0, 0, Math.max(0, n - vis)); if (this.i < first) first = this.i; else if (this.i >= first + vis) first = this.i - vis + 1; this._first = first;   // (the cursor's row in view)\n    const h = vis * rowH + (this.title ? rowH + 3 * k : 0) + 8 * k, x = this.x === 'center' ? Math.round((S.W - w) / 2) : this.x, y = this.y === 'center' ? Math.round((S.H - h) / 2) : this.y;\n    const top = y + 5 * k + (this.title ? rowH + 3 * k : 0); this._box = { x: x + 3 * k, y: top - 2 * k, w: w - 6 * k, rowH, first, vis };   // (where the entries are, for a click or tap)\n    return { labels, w, h, x, y, top, rowH, k, fo, first, vis };\n  }\n  /** entry i's box on the screen, [x, y, w, h] in screen pixels: where a click or tap picks it (a test's feed('down') and\n   *  feed('up') there); null while it is scrolled out of view */\n  rowAt(i) { this._layout(); const b = this._box; return i < b.first || i >= b.first + b.vis ? null : [b.x, b.y + (i - b.first) * b.rowH, b.w, b.rowH]; }\n  /** move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"455aabbf-dbfa-409a-91df-ba2177dd6342","uuid":"ebba88a9-996e-47fa-afe5-99eb360f7d3e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T12:57:31.049Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"198:- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dit\n199:- `px.col(g, c)`: set the fill color (px.* do it themselves)\n200:- `px.ddisc(g, cx, cy, r, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: soft disc that fades toward its edge (glows, smoke, dust): stepped alpha rings, or dithering in 'dither' style\n201:- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n202:- `px.dot(g, x, y, c)`: one pixel\n203:- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n204:- `px.glow(g, e = 1)`: GPU lighting: what follows glows (0..1). No effect in Canvas mode, so call it freely.\n205:- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n206:- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n207:- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel off\n208:- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n209:- `px.reset(g)`: forget the color cache (after drawing on g with the canvas API directly)\n210:- `px.sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip = false)`: draw a sprite with its top-left corner at buffer pixel (x, y). flip mirrors it left-right; or o: { flip, rot (radians, turn\n360:- `E.font.default` †: the font used when none is named: 'normal' (5 x 7) or 'tiny' (3 x 5)\n361:- `E.font.height(lines = 1, o, lineGap)`: the height in pixels of that many lines (with o's scale and font, and lineGap between them)\n362:- `E.font.lineHeight(o)`: pixels from one line to the next\n363:- `E.font.text(g, s, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o = '#0b0814')`: draw text at (x, y) (its top-left; align: 'center' or 'right' moves it) in color. o\n364:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D\n365:- `E.font.width(s, o)`: width in pixels of the widest line. opts: a scale number or { font, scale }\n366:- `E.font.wrap(s, maxW, o)`: split text into lines no wider than maxW pixels\n1179:- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0\n1180:- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-\n1181:- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n1182:- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)\n170:- `E.mkCanvas(w, h)`: a new canvas of w x h pixels (scratch images and sprite sheets). With no document (Node: a headless game) a stand-in whose drawing does nothing,\n191:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward wa\n283:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that d\n300:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n309:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns tr\n345:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n486:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Sh\n489:- `game.freeze(s)`: hit-stop: the game stands still for s seconds (.04-.08 for a hit); input still ticks\nclass Menu {\n  constructor(game, items, o = {}) {\n    /** game: its game; items: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled }); i: the one under the cursor; active:\n     *  false stops it reading input */\n    this.game = game; this.items = items || []; this.i = 0; this.active = true;\n    /** x, y: where it sits, 'center' or pixels; title: a heading, or null; box: draw a window round it; color: the\n     *  entries' color; pick: the color of the one under the cursor; dim: disabled entries' color; bg, border: the\n     *  window's colors; onPick: called (i, item) on confirm; onCancel: called on cancel; onMove: called (i, item)\n     *  when the cursor moves; sound: false silences it; input: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so\n     *  any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's); scale: its text and rows that many times (2, 3:\n     *  across a room on a TV); rows: at most that many entries shown, the list scrolling under its cursor (0: all) */\n    Object.assign(this, { x: 'center', y: 'center', title: null, box: true, color: '#ffffff', pick: '#ffd36a', dim: '#6a6488', bg: '#141a3a', border: '#e8e4ff', onPick: null, onCancel: null, onMove: null, sound: true, input: null, scale: 1,\n    this._skip(1);\n  }\n  _label(it) { return typeof it === 'string' ? it : it.label; }\n  _off(it) { return typeof it === 'object' && it.disabled; }\n  _skip(dir) { for (let k = 0; k < this.items.length && this._off(this.items[this.i]); k++) this.i = (this.i + dir + this.items.length) % this.items.length; }\n  /** the entry under the cursor */\n  get selected() { return this.items[this.i]; }\n  // where it sits, from its items and the screen's size (update and draw both: a click picks an entry with no draw yet)\n  _layout() {\n    const S = this.game.screen, k = Math.max(1, Math.round(this.scale || 1)), fo = { scale: k }, labels = this.items.map(it => this._label(it)), n = labels.length;\n    const w = Math.max(E.font.width(this.title || '', fo), ...labels.map(l => E.font.width(l, fo))) + 22 * k, rowH = E.font.lineHeight(fo) + 2 * k, vis = this.rows > 0 ? Math.min(n, this.rows) : n;\n    let first = clamp(this._first || 0, 0, Math.max(0, n - vis)); if (this.i < first) first = this.i; else if (this.i >= first + vis) first = this.i - vis + 1; this._first = first;   // (the cursor's row in view)\n    const h = vis * rowH + (this.title ? rowH + 3 * k : 0) + 8 * k, x = this.x === 'center' ? Math.round((S.W - w) / 2) : this.x, y = this.y === 'center' ? Math.round((S.H - h) / 2) : this.y;\n    const top = y + 5 * k + (this.title ? rowH + 3 * k : 0); this._box = { x: x + 3 * k, y: top - 2 * k, w: w - 6 * k, rowH, first, vis };   // (where the entries are, for a click or tap)\n    return { labels, w, h, x, y, top, rowH, k, fo, first, vis };\n  }\n  /** entry i's box on the screen, [x, y, w, h] in screen pixels: where a click or tap picks it (a test's feed('down') and\n   *  feed('up') there); null while it is scrolled out of view */\n  rowAt(i) { this._layout(); const b = this._box; return i < b.first || i >= b.first + b.vis ? null : [b.x, b.y + (i - b.first) * b.rowH, b.w, b.rowH]; }\n  /** move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NHhDFGyWvTTqMeqC7mhef1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
