1.6] }, shapes: [['crashcart', 12.4, 5.3], ['ivstand', 5, 1.2], ['kaykit-furniture-bits:cabinet-small', 8.5, 5.3]], lamp: true },\"\"\")\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nSI={\n \"date\":\"2026-11-05 05:40:07\",\n \"source\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)\",\n \"plan\":\"PLAN.md\",\n \"genre\":\"Surgical action game, with story scenes and a small walkable ward\",\n \"perspective\":\"First-person top-down on the operative field; front-on portrait stages for story; three-quarter view for the ward and cinematics; side view for the title\",\n \"tech\":\"my-3D2dge v0.89.1 (full engine, with one patch: the touch notice sits low so the attract reel shows above it), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio, one self-contained HTML file, no CDN\",\n \"artDirection\":\"The engine's pixel look at PS1 level: per-pixel wet tissue through hand-picked ramps with ordered dithering, flat-shaded bust portraits, painted stages, all by code; a few store props (Kenney, KayKit, CC0) for generic furniture\",\n \"animation\":\"The engine's Humanoid rigs and continuous-value animation, with new poses (scrub-in, gurney push, instrument pass, leaning over the table, knitting, shouting), a surgical cap, a mask and held objects; procedural organs, parasites and instruments; coroutine cinematics\",\n \"audio\":\"All in code on Web Audio: synthesized effects, a parasite choir on the effects bus, Animalese-style gibberish voices with formants per character, songs in the engine's notation with music at 10% by default\",\n \"online\":\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1 to 4 players, with the game's own card; couch co-op on its own (pads, keyboard halves, AI colleagues)\",\n \"testing\":\"Headless tools and scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count; screenshots only for what a script cannot check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit\",\n \"research\":\"The plan's own research was used (Wikipedia and a retrospective essay, as PLAN.md reports). No further research was done in this build.\",\n \"environment\":\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\",\n \"model\":\"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\",\n \"usage\":\"added on import\"}\njson.dump({\"sourceInformation\":SI,\"testingFeedback\":[\"pending\"]*4,\"engineFeedback\":[\"pending\"]*6,\"promptFeedback\":[\"pending\"]*4,\n\"aiHub\":{\"name\":\"Trauma Bender: Second Opinion\",\"tagline\":\"Don't let it go quiet\",\"description\":\"A rookie surgeon and a deadpan nurse race to save patients from a parasite that sings, in a hospital soap opera played with eight surgical tools. Alone, on one couch, or with up to four surgeons in a Hub session.\",\"type\":\"Game\",\"genre\":\"Simulation\",\"source\":\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\"series\":\"Trauma Center\",\"players\":\"1–4\",\"controls\":\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Pick tool: left stick or 1-8. Gift: Triangle or F\",\"tags\":[\"2d\",\"pixel art\",\"story\",\"co-op\",\"boss fights\",\"comedy\"]},\n\"credits\":[\"Trauma Bender: Second Opinion is an original work inspired by Trauma Center: Second Opinion, and is unaffiliated with it or its makers. Its story, characters, art, music and operations are its own.\",\"Built on my-3D2dge v0.89.1 by Michael Crosato (MIT License). AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0.\",\"Store props: Kenney Furniture Kit (kenney.nl), CC0 1.0. KayKit Furniture Bits (kaylousberg.com), CC0 1.0.\",\"Everything else, every picture, song, sound and voice, is drawn or synthesized by code. There are no image or audio files.\",\"Not a medical training tool. Please do not.\"]},open('src/about-data.json','w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=1)\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs; timeout 500 node tests/run.mjs --fast 2>&1 | tail -8 | cut -c1-500","description":"Rearrange the wards, write draft about data, run all headless tests","timeout":520000}}}
