{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjvCsKA6pv2SYbUA8rL9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UJNKzWFdMBGvF5dcmrtKDq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-054007__x488eb9/work/TraumaBenderSecondOpinion-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-054007\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ndef sub(p, a, b):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    if a not in s: print('MISSING', p, a[:90])\n    open(p,'w').write(s.replace(a,b,1))\nsub('src/scenes/hubround.js',\"Glyph.action(g, I, 'confirm', x + 14, by); E.font.text(g, rdy ? 'Ready!' : 'Ready', x + 34, by + 1, rdy ? '#117a74' : ink, f);\",\"const cw = Glyph.action(g, I, 'confirm', x + 14, by); E.font.text(g, rdy ? 'Ready!' : 'Ready', x + 18 + cw, by + 1, rdy ? '#117a74' : ink, f);\")\nsub('src/art/instruments.js',\"px.line(g, x + 13, y + 15, x + 130, y + 155, sl.deep, 11); px.line(g, x + 12, y + 14, x + 129, y + 154, sl.base, 9); px.line(g, x + 14, y + 13, x + 131, y + 153, sl.lt, 2);\",\"px.line(g, x + 13, y + 15, x + 330, y + 385, sl.deep, 11); px.line(g, x + 12, y + 14, x + 329, y + 384, sl.base, 9); px.line(g, x + 14, y + 13, x + 331, y + 383, sl.lt, 2);\")\nA=json.load(open('src/about-data.json'))\nA['testingFeedback']=[\n \"22 real issues, logged in notes/feedback.md as they were caught: 19 by scripts that play the game, 3 by looking at screenshots.\",\n \"7 would have been game breaking: a syringe tutorial that never cleared, a Code Blue that could not fire, a phase that soft-locked if a nest died early, a boss that could not be finished, a skipped cinematic hanging the campaign, an endless rewind loop in the finale, and a ward where the hero spawned stuck.\",\n \"The scripted full playthrough, New Game to credits through the real scenes with the bot's cheats off. A close second: driving Case 1 with real mouse events in a browser, which proved the hands work end to end.\",\n \"The view-cycling part of the engine's check tool: this game fixes its view per scene, so it only confirmed nothing. Its look note about the difficulty screen's color count was useful, though.\"]\nA['engineFeedback']=[\n \"The exact fixed step with game.advance and input.tap: the whole game runs headless in seconds, the same every time. Pause, settings, rebinding, glyphs and the TV shell came free and just worked.\",\n \"Yes, a few times. E.shade's amount is signed, and I guessed it the wrong way. input.lastDevice stays keyboard on a mouse move. A front wall hides a room until it has cut: true. Calling story.resume() inside its own event is silently lost.\",\n \"The operation sim: one JSON-safe state with eight tool gestures, strains, rewinds and checkpoints, plus the per-pixel tissue painter and the bot that plays through the real cursor path. None of that is an engine feature, and all of it is the game.\",\n \"Moving between views and scenes mid-story for cinematics: the view, camera bounds, lights and scene-scoped scripts each reset by different rules, and it took a hook on scene enter to make it tidy.\",\n \"Two patches. The touch notice sits low on the screen instead of covering it, so the attract reel shows above it (the plan's Appendix E). A mouse move now sets lastDevice to mouse from keyboard too, because hover must move the focus from the first move.\",\n \"Make story.resume() safe to call from inside the story's own event handler, or warn when it is ignored. It failed silently and hung the campaign.\"]\nA['promptFeedback']=[\n \"The plan's verified facts and exact numbers: the reference painters, the Hub skeleton and the harness runner saved rediscovery, and every tool's gesture came with numbers I could test.\",\n \"How to write GameTitle in a file name when the title has a colon and spaces: I used the compact form, TraumaBenderSecondOpinion. Also the plan's fact 7 on mouse devices, which only holds after a pad was used.\",\n \"Judging how the hands feel with no person to play: scripts and a bot can prove a stroke lands, not that it is fun. Case balance for real people is an estimate from bot runs.\",\n \"Allow one human playtest pass, or give a target for how much slower than a bot a first-time player is. Also state the file-name form for titles with punctuation.\"]\njson.dump(A,open('src/about-data.json','w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=1)\ns=open('notes/feedback.md').read()\ns=s.replace(\"## Engine surprises\\n\",\"19. Hover focus never engaged from a fresh start (engine's lastDevice rule; found by the ward's browser test).\\n20. The difficulty screen had a thin palette (the engine's check tool look note).\\n21. The forearm was a box bigger than the instrument (screenshot).\\n22. The Hub card's Ready label overlapped its key cap (screenshot).\\n\\n## Engine surprises\\n\",1)\nopen('notes/feedback.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -c \"^[0-9]*\\.\" notes/feedback.md; node tools/build.mjs -v; timeout 590 node tests/run.mjs --fast 2>&1 | tail -5 | cut -c1-400; python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print(list(d.keys()), d['aiHub']['name'], len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']))\"","description":"Write the feedback answers, rebuild and run headless tests","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1547,"cache_read_input_tokens":758982,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1547},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"455aabbf-dbfa-409a-91df-ba2177dd6342","uuid":"43c07ef3-ceb1-482c-a420-d5559bacd3f9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:13:04.900Z","request_id":"req_011CgjvCrv6TteKfdBM4ZxTA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UJNKzWFdMBGvF5dcmrtKDq":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-054007__x488eb9/work/TraumaBenderSecondOpinion-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-054007\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ndef sub(p, a, b):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    if a not in s: print('MISSING', p, a[:90])\n    open(p,'w').write(s.replace(a,b,1))\nsub('src/scenes/hubround.js',\"Glyph.action(g, I, 'confirm', x + 14, by); E.font.text(g, rdy ? 'Ready!' : 'Ready', x + 34, by + 1, rdy ? '#117a74' : ink, f);\",\"const cw = Glyph.action(g, I, 'confirm', x + 14, by); E.font.text(g, rdy ? 'Ready!' : 'Ready', x + 18 + cw, by + 1, rdy ? '#117a74' : ink, f);\")\nsub('src/art/instruments.js',\"px.line(g, x + 13, y + 15, x + 130, y + 155, sl.deep, 11); px.line(g, x + 12, y + 14, x + 129, y + 154, sl.base, 9); px.line(g, x + 14, y + 13, x + 131, y + 153, sl.lt, 2);\",\"px.line(g, x + 13, y + 15, x + 330, y + 385, sl.deep, 11); px.line(g, x + 12, y + 14, x + 329, y + 384, sl.base, 9); px.line(g, x + 14, y + 13, x + 331, y + 383, sl.lt, 2);\")\nA=json.load(open('src/about-data.json'))\nA['testingFeedback']=[\n \"22 real issues, logged in notes/feedback.md as they were caught: 19 by scripts that play the game, 3 by looking at screenshots.\",\n \"7 would have been game breaking: a syringe tutorial that never cleared, a Code Blue that could not fire, a phase that soft-locked if a nest died early, a boss that could not be finished, a skipped cinematic hanging the campaign, an endless rewind loop in the finale, and a ward where the hero spawned stuck.\",\n \"The scripted full playthrough, New Game to credits through the real scenes with the bot's cheats off. A close second: driving Case 1 with real mouse events in a browser, which proved the hands work end to end.\",\n \"The view-cycling part of the engine's check tool: this game fixes its view per scene, so it only confirmed nothing. Its look note about the difficulty screen's color count was useful, though.\"]\nA['engineFeedback']=[\n \"The exact fixed step with game.advance and input.tap: the whole game runs headless in seconds, the same every time. Pause, settings, rebinding, glyphs and the TV shell came free and just worked.\",\n \"Yes, a few times. E.shade's amount is signed, and I guessed it the wrong way. input.lastDevice stays keyboard on a mouse move. A front wall hides a room until it has cut: true. Calling story.resume() inside its own event is silently lost.\",\n \"The operation sim: one JSON-safe state with eight tool gestures, strains, rewinds and checkpoints, plus the per-pixel tissue painter and the bot that plays through the real cursor path. None of that is an engine feature, and all of it is the game.\",\n \"Moving between views and scenes mid-story for cinematics: the view, camera bounds, lights and scene-scoped scripts each reset by different rules, and it took a hook on scene enter to make it tidy.\",\n \"Two patches. The touch notice sits low on the screen instead of covering it, so the attract reel shows above it (the plan's Appendix E). A mouse move now sets lastDevice to mouse from keyboard too, because hover must move the focus from the first move.\",\n \"Make story.resume() safe to call from inside the story's own event handler, or warn when it is ignored. It failed silently and hung the campaign.\"]\nA['promptFeedback']=[\n \"The plan's verified facts and exact numbers: the reference painters, the Hub skeleton and the harness runner saved rediscovery, and every tool's gesture came with numbers I could test.\",\n \"How to write GameTitle in a file name when the title has a colon and spaces: I used the compact form, TraumaBenderSecondOpinion. Also the plan's fact 7 on mouse devices, which only holds after a pad was used.\",\n \"Judging how the hands feel with no person to play: scripts and a bot can prove a stroke lands, not that it is fun. Case balance for real people is an estimate from bot runs.\",\n \"Allow one human playtest pass, or give a target for how much slower than a bot a first-time player is. Also state the file-name form for titles with punctuation.\"]\njson.dump(A,open('src/about-data.json','w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=1)\ns=open('notes/feedback.md').read()\ns=s.replace(\"## Engine surprises\\n\",\"19. Hover focus never engaged from a fresh start (engine's lastDevice rule; found by the ward's browser test).\\n20. The difficulty screen had a thin palette (the engine's check tool look note).\\n21. The forearm was a box bigger than the instrument (screenshot).\\n22. The Hub card's Ready label overlapped its key cap (screenshot).\\n\\n## Engine surprises\\n\",1)\nopen('notes/feedback.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -c \"^[0-9]*\\.\" notes/feedback.md; node tools/build.mjs -v; timeout 590 node tests/run.mjs --fast 2>&1 | tail -5 | cut -c1-400; python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print(list(d.keys()), d['aiHub']['name'], len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']))\"","description":"Write the feedback answers, rebuild and run headless tests","timeout":600000}}}
