{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BwDmVUbRAwB7W812HDnPWh","type":"tool_result","content":"29 checks, 0 failed\ntotal 1928\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 06:38 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 05:40 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  130674 Nov  5 05:40 PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    2252 Nov  5 07:30 PROGRESS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     219 Nov  5 05:40 STAGE.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   12548 Nov  5 05:40 TASK.md\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 07:30 TraumaBenderSecondOpinion-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1794426 Nov  5 07:26 TraumaBenderSecondOpinion-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    6014 Nov  5 07:26 exit-interview.json\n{\n\"sourceInformation\": {\n\"date\": \"2026-11-05 05:40:07\",\n\"source\": \"Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)\",\n\"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n\"genre\": \"Surgical action game, with story scenes and a small walkable ward\",\n\"perspective\": \"First-person top-down on the operative field; front-on portrait stages for story; three-quarter view for the ward and cinematics; side view for the title\",\n\"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.89.1 (the full engine, with two small patches: the touch notice sits low so the attract reel shows above it, and a mouse move always sets the last device), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio, one self-contained HTML file, no CDN\",\n\"artDirection\": \"The engine's pixel look at PS1 level: per-pixel wet tissue through hand-picked ramps with ordered dithering, flat-shaded bust portraits, painted stages, all by code; a few store props (Kenney, KayKit, CC0) for generic furniture\",\n\"animation\": \"The engine's Humanoid rigs and continuous-value animation, with new poses (scrub-in, gurney push, instrument pass, leaning over the table, knitting, shouting), a surgical cap, a mask and held objects; procedural organs, parasites and instruments; coroutine cinematics\",\n\"audio\": \"All in code on Web Audio: synthesized effects, a parasite choir on the effects bus, Animalese-style gibberish voices with formants per character, songs in the engine's notation with music at 10% by default\",\n\"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1 to 4 players, with the game's own card; couch co-op on its own (pads, keyboard halves, AI colleagues)\",\n\"testing\": \"Headless tools and scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count; screenshots only for what a script cannot check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit\",\n\"research\": \"The plan's own research was used (Wikipedia and a retrospective essay, as PLAN.md reports). No further research was done in this build.\",\n\"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\",\n\"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\",\n\"usage\": \"added on import\"\n},\n\"testingFeedback\": [\n\"22, logged in notes/feedback.md as they were caught: 15 by scripts that play the game (one of those a bug in the test itself), 7 by looking at screenshots.\",\n\"7 would have been game breaking: a syringe tutorial that never cleared, a Code Blue that could not fire, a phase that soft-locked if a nest died early, a boss that could not be finished, a skipped cinematic hanging the campaign, an endless rewind loop in the finale, and a ward where the hero spawned stuck.\",\n\"The scripted full playthrough, New Game to credits through the real scenes with the bot's cheats off. A close second: driving Case 1 with real mouse events in a browser, which proved the hands work end to end.\",\n\"The view-cycling part of the engine's check tool: this game fixes its view per scene, so it only confirmed nothing. Its look note about the difficulty screen's color count was useful, though.\"\n],\n\"engineFeedback\": [\n\"The exact fixed step with game.advance and input.tap: the whole game runs headless in seconds, the same every time. Pause, settings, rebinding, glyphs and the TV shell came free and just worked.\",\n\"Yes, a few times. E.shade's amount is signed, and I guessed it the wrong way. input.lastDevice stays keyboard on a mouse move. A front wall hides a room until it has cut: true. Calling story.resume() inside its own event is silently lost.\",\n\"The operation sim: one JSON-safe state with eight tool gestures, strains, rewinds and checkpoints, plus the per-pixel tissue painter and the bot that plays through the real cursor path. None of that is an engine feature, and all of it is the game.\",\n\"Moving between views and scenes mid-story for cinematics: the view, camera bounds, lights and scene-scoped scripts each reset by different rules, and it took a hook on scene enter to make it tidy.\",\n\"Two patches. The touch notice sits low on the screen instead of covering it, so the attract reel shows above it (the plan's Appendix E). A mouse move now sets lastDevice to mouse from keyboard too, because hover must move the focus from the first move.\",\n\"Make story.resume() safe to call from inside the story's own event handler, or warn when it is ignored. It failed silently and hung the campaign.\"\n],\n\"promptFeedback\": [\n\"The plan's verified facts and exact numbers: the reference painters, the Hub skeleton and the harness runner saved rediscovery, and every tool's gesture came with numbers I could test.\",\n\"How to write GameTitle in a file name when the title has a colon and spaces: I used the compact form, TraumaBenderSecondOpinion. Also the plan's fact 7 on mouse devices, which only holds after a pad was used.\",\n\"Judging how the hands feel with no person to play: scripts and a bot can prove a stroke lands, not that it is fun. Case balance for real people is an estimate from bot runs.\",\n\"Allow one human playtest pass, or give a target for how much slower than a bot a first-time player is. Also state the file-name form for titles with punctuation.\"\n],\n\"aiHub\": {\n\"name\": \"Trauma Bender: Second Opinion\",\n\"tagline\": \"Don't let it go quiet\",\n\"description\": \"A rookie surgeon and a deadpan nurse race to save patients from a parasite that sings, in a hospital soap opera played with eight surgical tools. Alone, on one couch, or with up to four surgeons in a Hub session.\",\n\"type\": \"Game\",\n\"genre\": \"Simulation\",\n\"source\": \"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\n\"series\": \"Trauma Center\",\n\"players\": \"1–4\",\n\"controls\": \"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Pick tool: left stick or 1-8. Gift: Triangle or F\",\n\"tags\": [\n\"2d\",\n\"pixel art\",\n\"story\",\n\"co-op\",\n\"boss fights\",\n\"comedy\"\n]\n}\n}\n16M\tTraumaBenderSecondOpinion-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-054007/\n6","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"455aabbf-dbfa-409a-91df-ba2177dd6342","uuid":"3c834db5-e7c9-4a76-a25b-95cfb2180f05","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:30:42.213Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"29 checks, 0 failed\ntotal 1928\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 06:38 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 05:40 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  130674 Nov  5 05:40 PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    2252 Nov  5 07:30 PROGRESS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     219 Nov  5 05:40 STAGE.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   12548 Nov  5 05:40 TASK.md\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 07:30 TraumaBenderSecondOpinion-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1794426 Nov  5 07:26 TraumaBenderSecondOpinion-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    6014 Nov  5 07:26 exit-interview.json\n{\n\"sourceInformation\": {\n\"date\": \"2026-11-05 05:40:07\",\n\"source\": \"Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)\",\n\"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n\"genre\": \"Surgical action game, with story scenes and a small walkable ward\",\n\"perspective\": \"First-person top-down on the operative field; front-on portrait stages for story; three-quarter view for the ward and cinematics; side view for the title\",\n\"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.89.1 (the full engine, with two small patches: the touch notice sits low so the attract reel shows above it, and a mouse move always sets the last device), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio, one self-contained HTML file, no CDN\",\n\"artDirection\": \"The engine's pixel look at PS1 level: per-pixel wet tissue through hand-picked ramps with ordered dithering, flat-shaded bust portraits, painted stages, all by code; a few store props (Kenney, KayKit, CC0) for generic furniture\",\n\"animation\": \"The engine's Humanoid rigs and continuous-value animation, with new poses (scrub-in, gurney push, instrument pass, leaning over the table, knitting, shouting), a surgical cap, a mask and held objects; procedural organs, parasites and instruments; coroutine cinematics\",\n\"audio\": \"All in code on Web Audio: synthesized effects, a parasite choir on the effects bus, Animalese-style gibberish voices with formants per character, songs in the engine's notation with music at 10% by default\",\n\"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1 to 4 players, with the game's own card; couch co-op on its own (pads, keyboard halves, AI colleagues)\",\n\"testing\": \"Headless tools and scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count; screenshots only for what a script cannot check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit\",\n\"research\": \"The plan's own research was used (Wikipedia and a retrospective essay, as PLAN.md reports). No further research was done in this build.\",\n\"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\",\n\"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\",\n\"usage\": \"added on import\"\n},\n\"testingFeedback\": [\n\"22, logged in notes/feedback.md as they were caught: 15 by scripts that play the game (one of those a bug in the test itself), 7 by looking at screenshots.\",\n\"7 would have been game breaking: a syringe tutorial that never cleared, a Code Blue that could not fire, a phase that soft-locked if a nest died early, a boss that could not be finished, a skipped cinematic hanging the campaign, an endless rewind loop in the finale, and a ward where the hero spawned stuck.\",\n\"The scripted full playthrough, New Game to credits through the real scenes with the bot's cheats off. A close second: driving Case 1 with real mouse events in a browser, which proved the hands work end to end.\",\n\"The view-cycling part of the engine's check tool: this game fixes its view per scene, so it only confirmed nothing. Its look note about the difficulty screen's color count was useful, though.\"\n],\n\"engineFeedback\": [\n\"The exact fixed step with game.advance and input.tap: the whole game runs headless in seconds, the same every time. Pause, settings, rebinding, glyphs and the TV shell came free and just worked.\",\n\"Yes, a few times. E.shade's amount is signed, and I guessed it the wrong way. input.lastDevice stays keyboard on a mouse move. A front wall hides a room until it has cut: true. Calling story.resume() inside its own event is silently lost.\",\n\"The operation sim: one JSON-safe state with eight tool gestures, strains, rewinds and checkpoints, plus the per-pixel tissue painter and the bot that plays through the real cursor path. None of that is an engine feature, and all of it is the game.\",\n\"Moving between views and scenes mid-story for cinematics: the view, camera bounds, lights and scene-scoped scripts each reset by different rules, and it took a hook on scene enter to make it tidy.\",\n\"Two patches. The touch notice sits low on the screen instead of covering it, so the attract reel shows above it (the plan's Appendix E). A mouse move now sets lastDevice to mouse from keyboard too, because hover must move the focus from the first move.\",\n\"Make story.resume() safe to call from inside the story's own event handler, or warn when it is ignored. It failed silently and hung the campaign.\"\n],\n\"promptFeedback\": [\n\"The plan's verified facts and exact numbers: the reference painters, the Hub skeleton and the harness runner saved rediscovery, and every tool's gesture came with numbers I could test.\",\n\"How to write GameTitle in a file name when the title has a colon and spaces: I used the compact form, TraumaBenderSecondOpinion. Also the plan's fact 7 on mouse devices, which only holds after a pad was used.\",\n\"Judging how the hands feel with no person to play: scripts and a bot can prove a stroke lands, not that it is fun. Case balance for real people is an estimate from bot runs.\",\n\"Allow one human playtest pass, or give a target for how much slower than a bot a first-time player is. Also state the file-name form for titles with punctuation.\"\n],\n\"aiHub\": {\n\"name\": \"Trauma Bender: Second Opinion\",\n\"tagline\": \"Don't let it go quiet\",\n\"description\": \"A rookie surgeon and a deadpan nurse race to save patients from a parasite that sings, in a hospital soap opera played with eight surgical tools. Alone, on one couch, or with up to four surgeons in a Hub session.\",\n\"type\": \"Game\",\n\"genre\": \"Simulation\",\n\"source\": \"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\n\"series\": \"Trauma Center\",\n\"players\": \"1–4\",\n\"controls\": \"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Pick tool: left stick or 1-8. Gift: Triangle or F\",\n\"tags\": [\n\"2d\",\n\"pixel art\",\n\"story\",\n\"co-op\",\n\"boss fights\",\n\"comedy\"\n]\n}\n}\n16M\tTraumaBenderSecondOpinion-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-054007/\n6","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BwDmVUbR